{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "score": 0.13, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-005 | Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- observed_research_question: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.\n- observed_result: Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 523 cells; 440 pairs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "score": 0.12, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-058 | Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs\n- observed_research_question: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs\n- auto_outcome_status: rejected\n- observed_hypothesis: Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.\n- observed_result: 2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: null"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085", "score": 0.109, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-085 | Study family SF-APPS-085: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- observed_research_question: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) is a stable player-season attribute.\n- observed_result: Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Attenuation: even a perfect predictor  [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=102 connectors\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-086"}, {"id": "FAM:SF08", "score": 0.109, "document": "# FAM:SF08 | Study family SF08: Season adapter profiles: BEST-share vs playoff winning\n- observed_research_question: Season adapter profiles: BEST-share vs playoff winning\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Teams that consistently run more BEST-tier counters across seasons win more playoff series-directions.\n- observed_result: [APPA-051] Top BEST-share: BOS 15.7%/AVOID 21.4% Win 70% (10 dirs, 4 seasons); LAL 15.5%/23.1% Win 50% (6); OKC 12.3%/18.6% Win 89% (9 dirs, 3 seasons). Chronic AVOID: ORL 8.5%/59.3% Win 0% (3 dirs, 3 seasons).\n- observed_result: [APPS-039] Top mean BEST share: BOS 15.7% (10 dirs, win 70%), LAL 15.5%, GSW 13.8%. Bottom: HOU 2.5%, MIL 3.5%, LAC 4.1%. DEN 4.9% BEST / 70.8% INSUFF yet 62% win. ORL AVOID share 59.3%, 0% win.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF05"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
